        "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n#define TARGET_TILE 4\n#define PARALLEL_THRESHOLD 64\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/* Workshare target tiles while retaining the original ascending source order. */\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\n  long long block_count = ((long long)n + TARGET_TILE - 1) / TARGET_TILE;\n\n  #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n  for (long long block = 0; block < block_count; ++block) {\n    int base = (int)(block * TARGET_TILE);\n    int count = n - base;\n    if (count > TARGET_TILE) count = TARGET_TILE;\n\n    float tx[TARGET_TILE], ty[TARGET_TILE], tz[TARGET_TILE];\n    float fx[TARGET_TILE] = {0.0f};\n    float fy[TARGET_TILE] = {0.0f};\n    float fz[TARGET_TILE] = {0.0f};\n\n    for (int lane = 0; lane < count; ++lane) {\n      tx[lane] = p[base + lane].x;\n      ty[lane] = p[base + lane].y;\n      tz[lane] = p[base + lane].z;\n    }\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float xj = p[j].x;\n      float yj = p[j].y;\n      float zj = p[j].z;\n\n      #pragma omp simd\n      for (int lane = 0; lane < count; ++lane) {\n        float dx = xj - tx[lane];\n        float dy = yj - ty[lane];\n        float dz = zj - tz[lane];\n        float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n        float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n        float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n        fx[lane] += dx * inv_dist3;\n        fy[lane] += dy * inv_dist3;\n        fz[lane] += dz * inv_dist3;\n      }\n    }\n\n    for (int lane = 0; lane < count; ++lane) {\n      p[base + lane].vx += dt * fx[lane];\n      p[base + lane].vy += dt * fy[lane];\n      p[base + lane].vz += dt * fz[lane];\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  #pragma omp parallel if (nbodies >= PARALLEL_THRESHOLD) shared(bodies, nbodies)\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n      body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n        bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n        bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n  free(bodies);\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
        "path": "src/nbody.c"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Grouping four target bodies per statically scheduled work item and SIMD-processing those independent targets can reuse source coordinates and improve force-kernel throughput on the four-core ARM64 target. A single OpenMP team spans all iterations, while small inputs use a serialized team; each target still accumulates sources in ascending order.",
    "notes": "One bounded target-tile/worksharing experiment. Correctness and performance are unverified and remain controller-owned.",
